  "notes": "The research's phrase is \"more four-on-the-floor pull than the NY norm\", and that is the one parameter here that is not boom-bap: kick anchors on 1 and 3, `fourOnFloorInChorus` true, `syncopation` down to 0.22 and swing flattened to 0.53. The second distinctive is the open hat — offbeats on all four ands at `prob` 0.55 and up to four a bar, the highest in this batch. The third is that a sung counter-hook carries the melody, so `countermelody.densityRatio` is 0.55 and its register sits above the lead. ⚠ `medium` and the research marks the harmonic detail `[LOW-CONF]` explicitly — the INFERRED parameters are the chord families: i–VI–VII and I–V–vi–IV come from label-sound documentation rather than from any per-record analysis, and the i–iv and I–IV–V families at weight 2 are reductions of them rather than separately researched.",
